---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Shot from "../components/Shot.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import Marquee from "../components/Marquee.astro";
import { demoMailto } from "../data/site";
import overview from "../assets/product/package-overview.png";
import findings from "../assets/product/findings-queue.png";
import ask from "../assets/product/package-ask.png";

const title = "Rauzr — Dossiq for regulatory affairs";
const description =
  "Dossiq helps generic pharmaceutical regulatory teams check CTD Module 3 consistency for US CBE-30 and EU Type IB. Agents prepare the dossier. Humans file it.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="kicker">Dossiq · Decision support</p>
      <h1>Agents prepare the dossier.<br />Humans file it.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Dossiq checks CTD Module 3 across a generic variation — US CBE-30 and EU Type IB. Claims are extracted. Rules decide. Regulatory affairs files.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={demoMailto}>Request a demo</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/product/">See the product</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">Dossiq does not submit to FDA, EMA, or any other agency.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-stage">
      <Marquee />
      <div class="hero-frame">
        <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="hero-back" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="hero-shot">
          <Shot
            src={overview}
            eager={true}
            chrome="Dossiq · Package overview"
            alt="Dossiq package overview for a sample Stability Protocol Amendment. The screen shows zero blocking findings, two major findings open, one major waived, section completeness, a CTD Module 3 list with cross-checked and unverified rows, a Tier 1 source-document baseline, recent activity, and an Ask the package panel."
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fact-strip" aria-label="What Dossiq is built for">
    <div class="container">
      <dl class="fact-grid">
        <div>
          <dt>Pathway</dt>
          <dd>US CBE-30 and EU Type IB</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Dossier</dt>
          <dd>CTD Module 3 consistency</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Team</dt>
          <dd>Generic regulatory affairs</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Disposition</dt>
          <dd>Owned by the RA reviewer</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="gap-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head center">
        <p class="kicker">The gap</p>
        <h2 id="gap-title">Packages slip between documents.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          A specification, a method, a stability summary, and the last approved sequence can disagree while each file looks fine on its own.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-3">
        <article>
          <p class="index">01</p>
          <h3>Drift across the package</h3>
          <p>Drug substance specs, analytical validation, stability conclusions, and the regional letter are often read as separate files. Consistency is the second task, and it is easy to leave unfinished.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="index">02</p>
          <h3>A quote is not a decision</h3>
          <p>A language model can find a sentence and cite a page. The same package should produce the same check every time it is run. That belongs to a rule.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="index">03</p>
          <h3>A waiver has a name</h3>
          <p>When a finding is waived or a limit is accepted, the record needs the person, the rule, and the line in the source. Regulatory affairs can defend that.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" aria-labelledby="lanes-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head center">
        <p class="kicker">Judgment</p>
        <h2 id="lanes-title">Three kinds of work. Three owners.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Extraction can be a model. A pass or a fail is a rule, or it is a regulatory affairs reviewer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lanes">
        <article class="lane">
          <p class="index">01</p>
          <h3>Extract, with a page.</h3>
          <p>The model reads R&amp;D, QC, QA, and prior filings and pulls a claim only with a citation: document, page, and span. If it cannot cite, it does not answer.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="lane">
          <p class="index">02</p>
          <h3>Rules, the same result twice.</h3>
          <p>Deterministic checks compare those claims. The rule id is stored on the finding. The model does not vote on pass or fail.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="lane">
          <p class="index">03</p>
          <h3>Regulatory affairs disposes.</h3>
          <p>The queue shows source as Rule or Human. Agree, dispute, waive with a justification, or raise a finding yourself.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <aside class="aside-note">
        <p>
          <strong>Ask the package</strong> sits beside this flow. It reads the same sources and answers with citations. It does not open a finding, set a severity, or record a pass.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/approach/">Read the approach</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pull" aria-label="How Dossiq treats judgment">
    <div class="container">
      <blockquote>
        <p>Pass or fail is a rule, or it is a person.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <hr class="pull-rule" />
      <p class="pull-sub">Dossiq keeps those two sources of judgment separate, and named on the record.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 2rem" aria-labelledby="surfaces-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head center">
        <p class="kicker">In the product</p>
        <h2 id="surfaces-title">The review stays on one package.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Screens are the Dossiq interface with sample data. They are not customer work and not performance claims.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="surface">
        <div class="surface-copy">
          <p class="index">Queue</p>
          <h3>Findings the team can arbitrate.</h3>
          <p>Severity, CTD section, owner, and state sit on every row. Source is Rule or Human. The drawer keeps the rule id, the linked documents, and the thread.</p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li>Filter by severity, status, source, owner, and section</li>
            <li>Blocking, major, and minor stay distinct</li>
            <li>A waiver is logged with a justification</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="text-link" href="/product/#findings">Open the findings tour</a>
        </div>
        <Shot
          src={findings}
          chrome="Dossiq · Findings queue"
          alt="Dossiq findings queue for a sample package. Findings are listed with severity, CTD section, source marked Rule or Human, owner, and state. A detail drawer shows a rule id, linked documents, and a comment thread."
        />
      </div>

      <div class="surface reverse">
        <div class="surface-copy">
          <p class="index">Ask</p>
          <h3>Cite-only. No disposition.</h3>
          <p>Questions run across the package or a slice — a department, a batch, a document. Answers come back with the file and the page. Voice is another way to ask, with the same limits.</p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li>Every claim needs a document, page, and span</li>
            <li>Ask does not create findings or assign severity</li>
            <li>A readiness question is handed back to RA review</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="text-link" href="/product/#ask">See Ask on a package</a>
        </div>
        <Shot
          src={ask}
          scroll={true}
          chrome="Dossiq · Ask the package"
          alt="Dossiq Ask the package on a sample variation. A cited comparison table lists stability checks from R and D and QC with document and page. The screen labels an observation as not verified and refuses a readiness question, pointing to human review."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" aria-labelledby="guard-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head center">
        <p class="kicker">On the screen</p>
        <h2 id="guard-title">The product says this to the reviewer.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="quote-grid">
        <figure class="quote">
          <p>“Answers cite source documents only. Pass/fail comes from rules and RA review.”</p>
          <footer>Ask the package</footer>
        </figure>
        <figure class="quote">
          <p>“No severity. No auto-findings. Handoff to Raise finding when you want a disposition.”</p>
          <footer>Ask guardrail</footer>
        </figure>
        <figure class="quote">
          <p>“Ask never auto-creates findings. Voice is an input mode to this same chat.”</p>
          <footer>Ask the package</footer>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Base>
